### Block 5 - Relations and the owning side
### Select the "local" environment. Run the seed first (or create customers/products by hand).

### Sample data: change the numbers to grow or shrink the dataset
POST {{host}}/admin/seed?customers=5&products=5&salesPerCustomer=3&itemsPerSale=2

### Create a sale. Look at SaleService.create: sale.addItem(item) fills the foreign key.
### Also notice the stock decrement: there is no save() for the product.
POST {{host}}/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### Not enough stock -> 409 (the transaction rolls back, nothing is saved)
POST {{host}}/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 1000000 }
  ]
}

### List sales - NAIVE. Watch the console: count the SELECTs (we fix this in block 7)
### Q: how many queries for 15 sales?
GET {{host}}/sales

### Get one sale
GET {{host}}/sales/{{saleId}}

### Who owns the foreign key?
### Q: if I add the sale to customer.getSales(), does sales.customer_id change?
GET {{host}}/demo/owner-side?saleId={{saleId}}&newCustomerId={{newCustomerId}}
